WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.434
We're here with the one and only
Michelle Pfeiffer!

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:06.467
Now --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.701
In your new show,
"The First Lady,"

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.067
you play former First Lady
Betty Ford.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:15.133
-Mm-hmm.
-And I know you've played

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.701
actual people before.

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:22.067
Is it more pressure to play
someone who exists or existed?

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.634
-It is.
-Because why? The family?

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:28.100
-Well, I mean, to play,
you know,

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.934
somebody who is historical

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:34.334
and one of our most popular
First Ladies ever --

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.667
-Yeah.
-She's more popular

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:39.334
than Gerald Ford.
And, you know, she's --

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.467
There's family
that are still living.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:42.801
-Sure.
-And no matter --

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:44.734
And you kind of know that
no matter what you really do,

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:46.701
they're not gonna
like it so much.

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:48.567
-Yeah.
-You know? And you can't --

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.701
You can't be -- You want --

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:53.801
What you want to do
more than anything is honor her.

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:55.467
-Of course.
-And honor her legacy.

00:00:55.467 --> 00:01:02.033
-Yeah.
-And you can't be 100% accurate,

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.434
because nobody was there
100% of the time.

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.367
-Yeah, exactly.
-And so --

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.901
But I was lucky in that there
was a lot of footage of her.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.767
There was -- you know,
she did a lot of interviews.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:12.234
Of course, she gave speeches.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.167
-I don't really
know much about her, really.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:18.100
-Well, not many people do,
and that's what was so exciting.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.267
I mean, pretty much,

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.934
she's known for, you know,
the Betty Ford Clinic.

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:26.801
And she came out and she was
very vocal and very transparent

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:31.701
about her own drug abuse and her
substance abuse and alcoholism.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:35.634
And that's pretty much
kind of what people know.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.300
As if that weren't enough,
because she saved

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.701
hundreds of thousands of lives
with this clinic,

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:42.601
and continues to.
But she was --

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:45.567
What I didn't know was how
politically active she was.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.968
She was incredibly vocal,
always getting into trouble.

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:51.267
You know, she --
-Big trouble.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:52.901
-She was up to shenanigans.

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:57.467
She set up a command center

00:01:57.467 --> 00:02:00.367
in the White House to lobby

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:04.267
to get the
Equal Rights Amendment ratified.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.601
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.901
-You were saying backstage, too,
that, you know,

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:11.667
you realize how powerful
a First Lady is, actually.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.901
You know, what you can do
with that position.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:19.834
-Well, they're quietly --
they're quietly kind of working

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:23.234
their own agenda, of course,
supporting their husband's

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:24.701
and supporting the presidency

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:26.801
because that's really
what their job is.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:29.801
You know, they're out
always on the campaign trail.

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.367
They're always
campaigning for them.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:32.534
They're always --

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.167
Wherever the president can't go,
they'll show up.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:39.601
But they also -- you know,
they have their own voice.

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:42.467
And as she did.

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:45.701
And they're sort of
quietly working,

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.100
you know, behind the scenes.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.901
And this is really about,
you know,

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:54.400
looking at the White House
through the lens of these women.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.834
And, you know,
it's about Michelle Obama,

00:02:57.834 --> 00:03:00.234
played by Viola Davis.
-Viola Davis, come on.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:03.200
-And Gillian Anderson
plays Eleanor Roosevelt.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.667
-Another. Come on.
-And you know, it's --

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:08.067
And they're incredible.
-That's fantastic.

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.467
Three of you together --
This is just awesome.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.934
I want to show a clip.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:13.534
Here's Michelle Pfeiffer as
Betty Ford in "The First Lady."

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.767
Take a look at this.
-If you think I want

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.734
what's being handed to me
from this administration,

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:21.968
and I realize my ambitions
have made life hard for you,

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.367
but you knew what you were
getting into.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.868
-No.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:27.968
I did not know
what I was getting into.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.968
[ Clatters ]

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:37.601
But here I am.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:48.534
And I will be here for you.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.434
But I am going to be myself.

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:53.267
I am going to do and say things
that I believe in.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:55.667
I think I've earned that right.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.067
-Yeah.
That's how you do it.

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:58.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.434
That is how you do it.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:01.334
Michelle Pfeiffer, everybody.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:03.934
"The First Lady"
premieres April 17th

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:05.968
at 9:00 p.m. on Showtime.

